E711 [*] Comparison to `None` should be `cond is None`
  --> E711_E712_basedpython.by:12:16
   |
10 | # a lone comparison takes `is None`, a test for the type `None`, which holds one object
11 | def single(a: int | None, c: bool) -> None:
12 |     print(a == None)  # E711
   |                ^^^^
13 |     print(a != None)  # E711
14 |     print(c == True)  # E712
   |
help: Replace with `cond is None`
   |
11 | def single(a: int | None, c: bool) -> None:
   -     print(a == None)  # E711
12 +     print(a is None)  # E711
13 |     print(a != None)  # E711
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

E711 [*] Comparison to `None` should be `cond is not None`
